/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 36 0 R
/T (1. What is the difference between Git and GitHub? Git is a distributed version control system used to track changes in source code, documents, and project files. It helps developers manage different versions of a project and allows multiple people to work together efficiently. Git works on a local computer and keeps the history of all changes made in the project. GitHub is a cloud-based platform that hosts Git repositories online. It provides features like online storage, collaboration, project management, sharing repositories, and backup. GitHub allows developers to upload their local Git repositories to the internet so that team members can access and contribute to the project from anywhere. In simple words, Git is a tool for version control, while GitHub is a website or platform used to store and manage Git repositories online.)
/E (1. What is the difference between Git and GitHub? Git is a distributed version control system used to track changes in source code, documents, and project files. It helps developers manage different versions of a project and allows multiple people to work together efficiently. Git works on a local computer and keeps the history of all changes made in the project. GitHub is a cloud-based platform that hosts Git repositories online. It provides features like online storage, collaboration, project management, sharing repositories, and backup. GitHub allows developers to upload their local Git repositories to the internet so that team members can access and contribute to the project from anywhere. In simple words, Git is a tool for version control, while GitHub is a website or platform used to store and manage Git repositories online.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
